00:00.000  apparatus │ 
                      ── Plan: An ability then melee
                      
00:00.000  apparatus │   ~ The half of the 2026-08-09 note that nothing could check against a live world: after a hostile
                      ability lands, the Warden's *own weapon* should start swinging. Before the fix, `kick rat` hurt
                      the rat and left the player standing there — the mob was engaged and swung back, but nothing had
                      pointed the player's attacks at anything.
                      
                      It could not be observed because a level-1 Kick one-shots a city rat, so there was never anything
                      left to swing at. `ability-opens-a-fight` waits for whichever blow lands the kill and is honest
                      about not knowing which; this plan uses a target that cannot die to the opener, so the melee has
                      to show up.
                      
                      The dummy below is built by the apparatus before anyone plays: 400 health, no attacks, no
                      experience, and a sentinel spawner so it never wanders off. It hits nothing back, which is the
                      point — a plan that has to survive its own target is measuring the balance rather than the thing
                      under test. `npc` would make it unkillable *and* unattackable, so it is passive instead: the one
                      fixture in the set that has to be hittable.
00:00.058  Theron   │   ~ registered as playtest_uhbrzatu, playing Theronpewju the Warden
00:00.208  Theron   │   *(info) The Reaches hold, Theronpewju. Welcome back.
00:00.208  Theron   │   [hp 60/60 fp 20/20 sp 100/100 lvl 1 xp 0 gold 0]
00:00.208  Theron   │ The Gate Yard
                      The gate stands where it has always stood: a ring of dark stone twice the height of a man, set into the cobbles with no foundation and no seam. Nothing moves in it. Nobody living has seen anything move in it.
                      
                      Gatetown grew up around it anyway and treats it the way a town treats a large rock. Crates lean against the near side, children are told not to climb it, and the stone is worn shiny at shoulder height by three generations of people touching it on their way past.
                      
                      Yrriska's shrine sits at its foot — a bowl of coins, a knot of ribbon, and somebody's dice. It is the only untidy thing in the yard, and the sweepers go around it.
                      Exits: north, east, south, west
                      Hesper, who sweeps around the shrine is here.
